{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystonePivotalSpherical","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystonePivotalSpherical","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneRibbonMTCInput","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.Ribbon"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_twist_eq_leftQDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_twist_eq_leftQDim","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L312-L343","doc":"**The two traces differ by exactly the twist factor `θ_{Xᘁ} ⊗ θ_X`.**\n\nInserting that factor into the right trace produces the left trace on the nose. The proof\nis the Joyal–Street balancing axiom, which turns the double braiding into\n`θ_{Xᘁ ⊗ X}` dressed by the two component twists, followed by naturality of `θ` against\n`η ≫ β⁻¹ : 𝟙_C ⟶ Xᘁ ⊗ X` — which absorbs the whole `θ_{Xᘁ ⊗ X}`, since `θ_{𝟙} = 𝟙`.\n\n**This is why `ribbon ⇒ spherical` does not apply here.** The classical theorem concerns\nthe *twisted* trace, in which `θ` is already inserted; `qDimObj` and `leftQDim` are the\n*twistless* traces, and between those two the twist is not a normalisation but the entire\ndifference. A ribbon structure supplies `θ_{Xᘁ} = (θ_X)ᘁ`, which relates the factor's two\nhalves — it does not make the factor disappear. So sphericality is not a consequence of\nthe ribbon axiom for these definitions, and by `transport_iff_spherical` neither is\ntransport. Scope (a): this is a statement about *these* two definitions, not a claim that\nno twisted formulation closes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.pivotalTransport_of_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.pivotalTransport_of_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L288-L295","doc":"**In a symmetric right-rigid category the transport identity holds outright.**\n\n`leftQDim_eq_qDimObj_of_symmetric` proves sphericality there, and\n`transport_iff_spherical` converts it. So the hypothesis the conditional theorems above\ncarry is discharged for the whole symmetric class — the first unconditional case of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.pivotalTransport_of_spherical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.pivotalTransport_of_spherical","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L275-L279","doc":"**Sphericality supplies transport.** The half of the equivalence the conditional\ntheorems above actually consume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.transport_iff_spherical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.transport_iff_spherical","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L259-L273","doc":"**Pivotal transport and sphericality are equivalent**, unconditionally.\n\nThe factoring above presents them as two independent classical inputs. They are not\nindependent: modulo `QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_rightDual` (the unconditional conjugation\nsymmetry) each follows from the other in one rewrite.\n\nThe consequence is worth stating plainly. Transport is **not** unconditionally provable,\nbecause sphericality is not — the left and right traces genuinely differ in a general\nbraided rigid category, and a category where they agree is what *spherical* names. So the\nresidual recorded against this file was never two inputs of which one might fall; it is\none condition, wearing two names. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L241-L246","doc":"The same, drawing sphericality from the class rather than a bare hypothesis: in a\nspherical category only the pivotal transport remains. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport_of_spherical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport_of_spherical","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L221-L239","doc":"**The conjugation symmetry, conditional on the two standard inputs (§3b-cond).**\n\n`qDimObj (Xᘁ) = qDimObj X` follows from\n\n1. `hTransport` — the **pivotal transport** identity `qDimObj (Xᘁ) = leftQDim X`: the right\n   dimension of the dual is the left dimension of the object. This is the classical\n   pivotal statement; its proof is a string-diagram coherence argument and it is **not**\n   proved here (open, bean `rtqd`), carried as an explicit hypothesis rather than an\n   axiom; and\n2. `hSpherical` — **sphericality**, `leftQDim X = qDimObj X`, which\n   `leftQDim_eq_qDimObj_of_symmetric` **proves** in the symmetric case.\n\nNeither hypothesis is the conclusion — the conclusion is their composite. This is the\nhonest factoring of the gap the bean asked for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.qDim_conj_of_pivotalTransport_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L209-L215","doc":"**Symmetric case: the gap reduces to pivotal transport alone.** Sphericality is\ndischarged by `leftQDim_eq_qDimObj_of_symmetric`, so in a symmetric right-rigid category\nthe conjugation symmetry is exactly one classical lemma away. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.spherical_of_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.spherical_of_symmetric","kind":"instance","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L205-L207","doc":"The symmetric case as an instance: `SphericalStructure` is inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.leftQDim_eq_qDimObj_of_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.leftQDim_eq_qDimObj_of_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L196-L203","doc":"**Every symmetric right-rigid category is spherical.** The two traces are built from the\nsame coevaluation and evaluation, differing only in the crossing; symmetry identifies the\ntwo crossings, so `leftQDim = qDimObj`. Sorry-free and unconditional — this is the\nnon-vacuity witness for `SphericalStructure`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.braiding_inv_eq_hom_of_symmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.braiding_inv_eq_hom_of_symmetric","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L184-L194","doc":"In a symmetric category the inverse braiding **is** the forward braiding of the swapped\npair: `(β_ X Xᘁ).hom = (β_ Xᘁ X).inv`, directly from `SymmetricCategory.symmetry`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure.leftQDim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure.leftQDim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L169-L169","doc":"Left trace = right trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L166-L166","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.SphericalStructure","kind":"class","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L142-L169","doc":"**Sphericality**, in the standard form: the left and right quantum dimensions agree on\nevery object. (Equivalently, the left and right traces agree — here specialised to the\nidentity, which is the case the keystone consumes.)\n\n**Why this is a hypothesis and not a theorem, and when you do not need it.**\n\n`leftQDim` and `qDimObj` are the two *twistless* closures, and they differ by the monodromy\n`(β_ Xᘁ X).inv` against `(β_ X Xᘁ).hom`.  No axiom of a braided rigid category forces the\nmonodromy to vanish, so this class cannot be derived here — it is a genuine condition, which is\nwhat `spherical_of_symmetric` below witnesses from the other side (symmetric ⇒ monodromy trivial ⇒\nspherical).\n\nThe classical `ribbon ⇒ spherical` is a theorem about the **twisted** traces, and it does not reach\nthese two.  If a `BalancedCategory` is in scope, do not carry this hypothesis: use\n`QOU.MathlibExt.qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq`, which *proves* left = right for\n`qDimTwistedLeftWith` / `qDimTwistedWith` in any `RibbonCategory`.  Its companion\n`qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq_of_cap` shows the balancing axiom does all the geometric work and the\nribbon axiom is used exactly once, on the cap.\n\nSo the division of labour is: **this class is the right object precisely where there is no twist\navailable** — as here, where the variable block is braided right-rigid and no `θ` exists.  Where a\ntwist does exist, sphericality is a theorem and this class is the wrong thing to assume.  Nothing\nin this file needs migrating on that account: the results below are true at braided right-rigid\ngenerality, and requiring a ribbon structure to obtain them would be a loss, not a gain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.leftQDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PivotalSpherical.leftQDim","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystonePivotalSpherical.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**The left quantum dimension.** The mirror of `qDimObj`: the same coevaluation and\nevaluation, but crossing the strand with the **inverse** braiding `(β_ Xᘁ X).inv` instead\nof the forward `(β_ X Xᘁ).hom`. In a general braided rigid category the two traces differ;\na category in which they agree for every object is *spherical*. ","signatureChunk":0}]}